<title>INDIA: India's HDFC to raise foreign holding.</title>
<headline>India's HDFC to raise foreign holding.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's Housing Development Finance Corporation Ltd (HDFC) on Wednesday said its board had decided to allow raising of foreign institutional investment (FII) in its equity to 30 percent from 24 percent.</p>
<p>The government raised the cap on FII holding in Indian firms to 30 percent from 24 percent in its 1997/98 (April-March) budget, subject to the consent of a company's board.</p>
<p>HDFC, India's leading housing finance company, has been a favourite of overseas investors.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
